#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105521 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105926 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0aaf960-68e6-52a2-aed5-3e8cfc5c518e" :knowledge-point/title "Understanding Line Segment Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "4349d9b1-6a58-5c35-8cc1-14526f7cea4e" :question/math-academy-id "e-2546" :question/problem "Suppose that a line segment has a length of $2\\,\\textrm{m},$ and that $A$ and $B$ are its endpoints. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\overline{AB} = 2\\,\\textrm{m}$\n\nII. $\\overline{BA} = 2\\,\\textrm{m}$\n\nIII. $AB = 2\\,\\textrm{m}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The notation $\\overline{AB}$ represents the line segment itself, not the length of the line segment. Therefore, the expression ${\\overline{AB}}=2\\,\\textrm{m}$ is not valid. Instead, it should say $AB = 2 \\, \\textrm{m}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\overline{BA}$ represents the line segment itself, not the length of the line segment. Therefore, the expression ${\\overline{BA}}=2\\,\\textrm{m}$ is not valid.\n\n- Statement III is true. The notation $AB$ represents the length of the line segment $\\overline{AB},$ and this line segments has a length of $2\\,\\textrm{m}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB = 2\\,\\textrm{m}\n$$\n\nis a correct statement.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105522 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105927 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c92ac26-24aa-5b82-8689-a30b23f05bfe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Measure of a Line Segment on a Grid"}] :question/id #uuid "cfe017f1-09b7-52c4-88aa-bd312833173d" :question/math-academy-id "e-2547" :question/problem "What is the measure of the line segment $\\overline{ML}$ shown below?\n\n![](images/59/5956f2c41cb04f89e72602ec69ab76e729a3c031bd307f31bbcc24c7f12744ba.png)" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of a side of one cell is \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{10\\,\\textrm{mm}}{2} = 5\\,\\textrm{mm}.\n$$\n\nThe line segment has a length of $7$ cells, so the total measure is \n\n$$\nML = 7 \\cdot 5\\,\\textrm{mm} = 35\\,\\textrm{mm}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105523 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105928 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2b7b354-5f1a-5411-8dde-4255f14b127b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Measure of a Line Segment Using a Ruler"}] :question/id #uuid "b84a586f-47d6-5543-a751-f0aeaa53fd91" :question/math-academy-id "e-2549" :question/problem "The ruler shown below allows measuring length both in $\\textrm{cm}$ (centimeters) and $\\textrm{in}$ (inches). Determine the measure of the line segment $\\overline{MN}.$\n\n![](images/e1/e1d80c4344e4051f1b58a8c7ec1db9930f06d679c1a0532e83bfc7bdb719c4c1.png)" :question/worked-solution "Note that $M$ is not aligned with the zero-mark on the ruler. \n\nTo find the length, we read the values that correspond to the points $M$ and $N,$ and take the difference.\n\nFrom the picture, we see that $M$ corresponds to $0.5\\,\\textrm{in}$ while $N$ corresponds to $2\\,\\textrm{in}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}MN=2\\,\\text{in}-0.5\\,\\text{in}=1.5\\,\\text{in}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105524 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105929 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f186459-7a3c-5131-9696-5ce158911634" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Measure of a Line Segment on a Number Line"}] :question/id #uuid "620afc7e-0778-5778-8130-7dbe55680002" :question/math-academy-id "e-2550" :question/problem "Find the length of the line segment $\\overline{AB}$ shown below.\n\n![](images/aa/aa8af70fcbd81823439ba7a7919b68ac0814776a0cd5afce48162f40b6067061.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the length, we read the values that correspond to the points $A$ and $B$ and take the difference.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that $A$ corresponds to $10$ units while $B$ corresponds to $50$ units.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\nAB = 50 - 10 = 40\\,\\textrm{units}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105927 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c92ac26-24aa-5b82-8689-a30b23f05bfe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Measure of a Line Segment on a Grid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03170d95-31f2-5da2-aa85-7c107c5b9773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.25\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446095} {:answer/id #uuid "05b96e9a-3e82-5e77-b97f-219a5a16bbad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.75\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446096} {:answer/id #uuid "8c17b7b5-88f8-5ab3-9c4d-5567ad55dad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.25\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446121} {:answer/id #uuid "e789d5c3-4097-5c1b-a2ec-568a87394e8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.75\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446136} {:answer/id #uuid "eadbc7c1-bf63-5665-81cb-c57ed0805358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05b96e9a-3e82-5e77-b97f-219a5a16bbad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.75\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446096} :answer-field/id #uuid "37fa4f73-4b6f-5abb-85c5-3b635c0f9e1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446139}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b5924f6-1b4f-5cd0-89f3-79b22bdc59d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-113157" :question/problem "![](images/2f/2f148af3e47726793c57ad48ab608d90fb8378da4651973c2ba864f54633e2b4.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of the line segment $\\overset{―}{MN}$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of a side of one cell is \n\n$$\n\\frac{1\\,\\text{in}}{4}=0.25\\,\\text{in}.\n$$\n\nThe line segment has a length of $7$ cells, hence the total measure is \n\n$$\nMN=7\\cdot 0.25\\,\\text{in}=1.75\\,\\text{in}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446148 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105928 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2b7b354-5f1a-5411-8dde-4255f14b127b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Measure of a Line Segment Using a Ruler"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13ab330c-b10b-5ede-b50b-b9b2819b4f12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446101} {:answer/id #uuid "3fd9caae-c795-5ecf-ac67-5e1c80a1e7d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446109} {:answer/id #uuid "4cddb303-0487-5754-9529-4a124d16f998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446114} {:answer/id #uuid "5f7e780a-4216-5f56-bc95-fb5d7ee2346e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446116} {:answer/id #uuid "fce7b3e1-74ac-55b6-83bc-eb1b379570df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13ab330c-b10b-5ede-b50b-b9b2819b4f12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5\\,\\text{in}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446101} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8d1f117-e2ef-53ef-86d3-575132895d0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446143}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "13ca1ca9-18d5-5bc5-a895-698275236baa" :question/math-academy-id "q-113186" :question/problem "![](images/b9/b9e5d7d183fb090b317bd134829affc63792fbe88945941d5be1311e27751afb.png)\n\nDetermine the measure of the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "Note that $A$ is not aligned with the zero-mark on the ruler. \n\nTo find the length, we read the values that correspond to the points $A$ and $B,$ and take the difference.\n\nFrom the picture, we deduce that $A$ corresponds to $2\\,\\text{in}$ while $B$ corresponds to $3.5\\,\\text{in}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB=3.5\\,\\text{in}-2\\,\\text{in}=1.5\\,\\text{in}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446151 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105926 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0aaf960-68e6-52a2-aed5-3e8cfc5c518e" :knowledge-point/title "Understanding Line Segment Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e959fa5-8b29-5607-9d43-2eadc057ddb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446106} {:answer/id #uuid "40e95413-e09d-56c8-8429-95b89c3e104b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446110} {:answer/id #uuid "41dae19a-3d1e-5205-b6d7-7d5ead048a21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446111} {:answer/id #uuid "b19b68f1-5299-5a47-9d9a-713b9cee64c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446123} {:answer/id #uuid "e312ad0f-01d3-5aba-880c-ee952aa7d0e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218